      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This application discloses a series of di- and tri-substituted cyclohexanes as CCR2 receptor antagonists which are stated to be useful in treating inflammation and autoimmune diseases, such as type 2 diabetes and asthma. Although receptor binding of the compounds to CCR2 is demonstrated, there are no data to support the idea that these molecules are functional antagonists."},
